(THG2-07: a text initializer is a different sink - it builds its bytes in a
 buffer - so interpolating a whole thing there is rejected, and the message
 names the fields to interpolate instead. The buffer sink was run by hand from
 the same shape - `copy "{origin}" to rendered.` into a sized buffer - and gives
 the identical diagnostic, so no sink but `Print` can render a whole thing.
 That is why THG2-01, THG2-03, THG2-04 and THG2-06 are marked unassertable
 from inside a Vox program: there is no way to capture the rendering and
 compare it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG2-07.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: 'origin' holds a whole point, which only `Print` can interpolate
   followed by "Interpolate a field instead - point's fields are: x, y".
   No binary is produced; this is a compile error.
)
A thing called point has
  a number called x is 0,
  a number called y is 0.

a point called origin.
a text called note is "the point is {origin}".
